<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frank Swettenham</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1850">1850</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frank Swettenham was a British colonial administrator in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a>. Fluent in Malay, he served as Resident of Selangor and Perak and, in 1896, became the first Resident-General of the Federated Malay States, which he had helped design. From 1901 to 1904 he was Governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straits-settlements">Straits Settlements</a> and High Commissioner for the Malay States.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frank-swettenham.jpg" alt="Frank Swettenham" width="320" height="583" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Singer Sargent · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Frank_Swettenham_by_John_Singer_Sargent_1904.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
